{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341338-fan-made-courts-any-ideas-you-have-or-want-to-see","id":341338,"title":"Fan-Made Courts: Any ideas you have or want to see?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-15T16:54:02-08:00","id":341338,"title":"Fan-Made Courts: Any ideas you have or want to see?","content":"So, I think it's been a while since the last ones of these. So, as the title suggests, any ideas for Court and their Freeholds that you've heard of or come up with? I'll start;<br /> <br /> ~Moon Courts: Inspired by an idea I read in an RPG.net thread, the idea is that this Freehold was heavily influenced by the prelevant local Forsaken, who've alied with them in exchange for favors. Each Court represents a Moon phase(some would even say Auspice), and change when the phases do. What I have so far:<br /> \u2022New Moon<br /> \u2022Crescent Moon(Revelation)- Court of Shamans<br /> \u2022Half-Moon(Serenity)-Court of Counselors<br /> \u2022Gibbous Moon(Glory)-Court of Bard<br /> \u2022Full Moon<br /> <br /> ~Zodiac Courts: Inspired by the same thread as above, I'm not sure about the exact courts themselves(not an astrologer), but I know how the Freehold itself might be run. Each Monarch would, besides managing their subjects, serve on a Senate made of the 12 Courts to govern the Freehold itself. While it has theoretically unlimited power, it is hamstrung by the constant rivalries and politicking of its members and the Ophiuchus, a Changeling who is elected by the Freehold's people and who serves their intrests alone, such that he loses his Mantle while in office.<br /> <br /> ~Heavenly Courts: In a previous thread on the subject here, someone suggested a aet of Courts based on the 7 deadly sins and Dante's Inferno. I had the idea for the exact opposite; a group of Changelings who decided that, if They are repeled by Human Nature and are inherently wicked and cruel, then it might be best to claim the 7 Heavenly Virtues as patrons. Eqch rules over a day of the week, and claims as it's patron a Archangel, though individuals(often pious they may be, though there's not exactly a dearth of atheists) vary in weather or not they believe them actual Archangels. May switch Humility for Clarity; after all, they're really the same thing, and the later might be more needed by the Lost. The Courts:<br /> \u2022Charity-Sunday's Court, Michael's Court<br /> \u2022Kindness-Monday's Court, Gabriel's Court<br /> \u2022Humility- Tuesday's Court, Raphael's Court<br /> \u2022Chastity- Wednesday's Court, Uriel's Court<br /> \u2022Temperance- Thursday's Court, Cassiel's Court<br /> \u2022Diligence- Friday's Court, Jegudiel's Court<br /> \u2022Patience- Saturday's Court, Barachiel's Court<br /> <br /> Anyone else have any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T17:22:08-08:00","id":341391,"title":"","content":"I still have short writeups for the Private Court (aka The Ebon Court, The Private Court, The Golden Sword, The Court of Diamonds, The Court of Avarice) and the Public Court (aka The Scarlet Court, The Public Court, The Steel Clock, The Court of Clubs, The Court of Suspicion) sitting on my phone somewhere, for all that they were basically gimmicks tying together their Mantles and Social Merit dickery mixed with complementary signature token-types and capitalism/communism motifs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T17:26:54-08:00","id":341395,"title":"","content":"I have a &quot;jokey&quot; idea of making four Chaos courts, where they would be based off of the Chaos Gods. Shouldn't be that hard; Slaanesh is Spring by any other name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T17:50:08-08:00","id":341403,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the only really weird match-up there is Nurgle as Winter...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T17:59:02-08:00","id":341410,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Papa Nurgle is too friendly to be Winter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T18:24:15-08:00","id":341416,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I'd like to see courts that would fit in some of those other settings one might have a nwod game.<br /> <br /> Like some hi tech courts for a bleeding edge game, in an archology there might not be seasons, so it might be I don't know the courts of electricity, steel, blood (biotech), etc, <br /> <br /> Or in an infinite macabre game the court of stars, the comet court, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Hmm, apocalypse settings? After all there could be a nuclear winter. Perhaps changelings reduced to a more primitive existence would forge pacts with forces that would help them survive: courts of water, fire, wood, and the hunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T19:15:39-08:00","id":341458,"title":"","content":"Interesting ideas, all. <br /> <br /> @Satchel: Might be cool to see. <br /> <br /> @Amechra<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />on't know anything about Warhammer, so nothing I can say.<br /> <br /> @StSword: Good thought! The Rpg.net thread had a poster named Viatos named 3 Courts for this &quot;Infinite Macabre&quot; thing. They were:<br /> \u2022Court of Void, the Black Door: Alienation.<br /> \u2022Court of Stars, the Shining Net: Wonder.<br /> \u2022Court of Worlds, the Perfect Marble: Security.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T19:49:30-08:00","id":341470,"title":"","content":"I still need to work on my Prismatic Court scheme, where each Court represented a different color of the rainbow. . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T19:53:40-08:00","id":341471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341338-fan-made-courts-any-ideas-you-have-or-want-to-see?p=341470#post341470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still need to work on my Prismatic Court scheme, where each Court represented a different color of the rainbow. . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Why did the opening strains of <i>Moonlight Densetsu</i> immediately pop into my head?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T21:58:51-08:00","id":341559,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see a circus-based Freehold alternating between the Court of the Road (worry) while travelling and the court of the Ring (wonder) while in place for performances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T07:37:11-08:00","id":341874,"title":"","content":"I have a partial writeup for an Alchemical freehold. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In short: <br /> <br /> Changing one's own court is a must in order to complete one's own alchemical journey. <br /> <br /> <b>Court of Coke (Nigredo) - Regret. </b><br /> The courtiers of coke (Crows) analyze their bonds with the human word, and cut those that are not important enough. <br /> When a courtier cut all the bonds which he consider useless, she asks for a Murder - if the other courtiers thinks she is ready to become a Courtiers of Fries, they kiss her. <br /> Otherwise, they stab her. <br /> <br /> <b>Court of Fries (Albedo) - Challenge.</b><br /> The Courtiers of Fries (Doves) are prompted to search some new ability or side of themselves, by backpacking around, studying, enduring pain or learning from magic and others.<br /> When a Dove thinks he's learned enough, they swear the Peacock's Oath - that is, to speak &quot;the truth, all the truth, only the truth&quot; and become courtiers of Burger.<br /> <br /> <b>Court of Burger (Rubedo) - Pride</b><br /> The Courtiers of Burger are the rulers of the Freehold. They celebrate they own being in fullness, without hiding their vices, failures or beauties. <br /> In addition, they widen the influence of the Freehold - introduce and teach new changelings, write archives, build new connections or buildings for the Freehold...<br /> <br /> When they fail to uphold the Peacock's Oath (everyone knows how taxing it could be), they cease to be phoenix, and begin again their alchemic circle in the Coke Court. <br /> <br /> <br /> (If you wish to see the full writeup, i can post it or send it by pm)<br /> __________________________________________________ ___________<br /> <br /> I remember also someone did an excellent writeup based on Card Suits (Spades, Diamonds, Clubs, Hearts)<br /> <br /> King's Raven had also a nice idea for a Court System based on flowers whose king was a mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T08:01:29-08:00","id":341891,"title":"","content":"@Baroqo: &quot;I remember also someone did an excellent writeup based on Card Suits (Spades, Diamonds, Clubs, Hearts)&quot; <br /> If, my good sir, you refer to the Courts of Chance on Rpg.net, then I just posted a link to them in the homebrew thread yesterday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T20:48:43-08:00","id":342571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341338-fan-made-courts-any-ideas-you-have-or-want-to-see?p=341471#post341471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u2026Why did the opening strains of <i>Moonlight Densetsu</i> immediately pop into my head?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. Sailor Moon doesn't actually have a rainbow theme :P Though all the colors of the rainbow ARE accounted for at one point or another. . . .<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, if you ever get around to finishing your Private/Public Courts, I'd definitely be interested in looking at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","user":"Murder-chan","date":". 12-16-2014, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T21:13:21-08:00","id":342580,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm sorry, I love the idea, but;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroqo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Court of Coke</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Court of Fries</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Court of Burger</b></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">...Are we </span></span></span><i>sure </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">these aren't the Courts of Fast Food? </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T21:47:49-08:00","id":342596,"title":"","content":"I already had a fan made courts topic, but it's on page 2. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, people seemed to like it before, so here's my repost of the Bright Courts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Bright Courts:</b> The Bright Courts are comprised of Dark, Light, and Shadow. Unlike the Seasonal Courts who voluntarily share power with the passing of the year, the Bright Courts have very conflicting ideals and are known to battle each other constantly in an effort to gain power and influence within the Free Holds. The name Bright Courts refers to being named after varying degrees of light.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dark Court:</b> What's the best way to defeat your enemy? Turn their own power against them, or so the Dark Court's philosophy would claim. True Fae are some of the most twisted, cruel, and malevolent beings in creation, and the Dark Court seek to harness that evil for their own protection. Despite constantly being accused of being evil or being no better than the Gentry themselves, members of the Dark Court would disagree. While they are certainly not on good terms with outsiders, they do have the protection of their members at heart. Indeed, those who join the Dark Court may find that they are shockingly hospitable for a society who's passing often leaves death and destruction in its wake. The Dark Court is primarily concerned with the survival of the Dark Court, and anyone who refuses to join them is little more than a pawn at best. Becoming a member of the Dark Court means dedicating yourself to a life of self indulgence where you survive by your strength, wits, and the desire to do whatever it takes to survive.<br /> <br /> The Dark Court feeds off Selfishness, finding it much easier to harvest Glamour from those who care more about their own well being than how others might feel about the situation. The Dark Court is primarily concerned with the survival of the Dark Court. Everyone else is there to be used, exploited, and ultimately discarded when they are no longer of any worth. They coax society into acting on their selfish impulses such as greed, lust, anger, and so on. Members of the Dark Court often blend in with the criminal elements of society including local street gangs and organized crime, and they often set up their base in places where one can not afford to be generous if they hope to survive. Such behavior warrants them a very unpopular reputation among outsiders, but those who actually join the Court realize they're just trying to survive in a cruel and disorienting world. They will gladly endure the slings and arrows of their fellow Lost, so long as they can remain free another day. Because they have so little friends in which to call upon, the Dark Court members are surprisingly pleasant towards one another, helping each other out when they're not otherwise preying upon society's foolishness.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Dark Court contracts are Creeping Darkness, Encompassing Darkness, and Fading Darkness.<br /> <br /> <br /> Creeping Darkness are the subtle offensive powers of the Dark Court. It gives them the power to influence the minds of others by stoking their negative emotions and desires, making them more susceptible to carrying them out. Creeping Darkness is often used to make harvesting Glamour easier when wielded by less experienced Dark Courtiers, but in the hands of a veteran, it can be truly frightening.<br /> <br /> <br /> Encompassing Darkness are the blatant offensive powers of the Dark Court. It gives them the power to control darkness as if it were physical matter, attacking one's foes with tendrils of shadow being just one of its more basic powers. At the higher levels of mastery, some Dark Courtiers can even summon forth creatures made of living darkness to aid them in battle!<br /> <br /> <br /> Fading Darkness are the defensive powers of the Dark Court and primarily deal with stealth and trickery. Its name comes from the idea that there are times when it is best to avoid conflict rather than exasperate it. Fading Darkness can grant them the power to move unseen through the world, provided they do not attempt to interact with it in any significant way, and is primarily used as a means to escape from dangerous situations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Light Court:</b> The antithesis of the Dark Court, who have dedicated their lives to preserving all that the True Fae would corrupt. Firm believers in the idea that the end doesn't always justify the means, the Light Court preaches that evil can not be defeated by resorting to evil methods. To this end, they strive to maintain whatever remains of generosity, compassion, and mercy they have left, and do not allow the memories of their durances to corrupt their spiritual purity. While the Dark Court may have a reputation for being universally evil, the Light Court has a reputation for being universally good. However just as with the Dark Court, their reputation is not all its cracked up to be. Those who join the Light Court may find that their dedication to purity can be rather stifling at times. While they are not fanatical zealots who threaten harsh punishments upon those who defy them, they also do not take kindly to selfish indulgences such as base lust, greed, anger and so on. Their society is like an order of pious monks who reject the temptations of the earthly realm in order to strengthen their spirits against the forces of evil. Those who's willpower is not strong enough for such a devout lifestyle often find they can not live up to the Light Court's expectations, and inevitably drop out.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Light Court feeds on Selflessness, and they find a much easier time harvesting Glamour from those who bare compassion, kindness, and understanding towards others. They shun violence at least when they are the only ones in danger, but when the innocent are at risk, they will sadly resort to such methods to protect them. Their goal is to strengthen the souls of not only themselves but that of society as well, making their spirits nearly unbreakable when the True Fae come to claim them. Hoping to lead the world by example, they give those around them something to aspire towards. When in their mortal disguises, they often take on forms of people who are skilled at helping others such as doctors, open minded clergymen, therapists, and guidance councilors.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Light Court contracts are Dim Lighting, Brilliant Lighting, and Soothing Lighting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dim Lighting are the offensive powers of the Light Court and the name is derived from the idea that by resorting to violence, their light diminishes. Dim Lighting teaches the Light Court how to channel the forces of light into concentrated energy with the power to repel one's enemies. Only the highest levels of Dim Lighting possess actually lethal capabilities however, as killing one's enemies is only to be used as a last resort according to the Light Court's philosophy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Brilliant Lighting are the defensive powers of the Light Court and the name is derived from the idea that by embracing the way of peace, they can withstand any punishment. Brilliant Light channels the energy of the Light Court into protective barriers, and empowers the body to make it better capable of withstanding assaults. A master of Brilliant Lighting can be practically untouchable, evading or blocking the enemy's attacks until their spirit for battle is broken or satiated.<br /> <br /> <br /> Soothing Lighting are the support based powers of the Light Court and the name is derived from the fact that they use these powers to spread their philosophy. Soothing Light has abilities which can heal injuries, and disperse aggression from others. It enhances their social talents to find a more political way to resolve situations than swinging a sword at your foe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Court:</b> Adhering to the philosophy that putting all your faith in one ideal leads to destruction, the Shadow Court takes a mixture of Dark and Light Court teachings. Most of them are those who abandoned the previous two Courts when they found they were unable to adhere to their extremist views on how to combat the True Fae. The Shadow Court sees their strict devotion to good and evil methods to be foolish. What happens if your philosophy fails, or your enemies find a weakness and begin to exploit it? The Gentry are unpredictable and incomprehensible, and the only way to fight against them effectively is to be as flexible as possible. Plans rarely survive first contact, so it pays to have contingencies in place, and then it pays to have contingencies for those contingencies!<br /> <br /> The Shadow Court feeds on Adversity, and they find a much easier time harvesting Glamour from those who have a strong will and creative mind, who are able to overcome the many challenges that life has to offer. They use their powers in an effort to help others grow and prosper by finding new ways to defeat their obstacles whether physical or metaphysical. Among the three Courts mentioned, the Shadow Court is perhaps the one that is most loosely organized. Each member of the Shadow Court follows their own set of moral code, ethics, and ambitions. This makes the entire court unpredictable, but is also makes them incredibly diverse. Since they do not have a unified goal in mind beyond simply being able to overcome all odds, the True Fae find it very difficult to prey upon their desires and coerce them into servitude. Their desires are random with each member, and it can be a time consuming and expensive process to seduce more than a handful of Shadow Courtiers at a time. Their lack of unity is their greatest defense against those who would exploit their society!<br /> <br /> <br /> The Shadow Court contracts are Faded Shadow, Warped Shadow, and Splintered Shadow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Faded Shadow are the defensive powers of the Shadow Court and they are named after shadows which appear to be transparent due to the intensity of light around them. As with Brilliant Light, Faded Shadows abilities have protective capabilities that can bolster the user's defense against enemy attacks, but unlike their counterpart, they have a slightly more offensive approach to simply creating an impenetrable defense.<br /> <br /> <br /> Warped Shadow are the offensive powers of the Shadow Court and they are named after the event of a shadow altering its size and shape based on the form and direction of the light that is shining upon it. Warped Shadow teaches the Shadow Court various shapeshifting powers from size alteration to sprouting claws and even changing their appearance completely for a certain amount of time. With the ability to alter their forms like shadow puppets, the Shadow Court are able to quickly adapt to almost any combat situation!<br /> <br /> <br /> Splintered Shadow are the social based powers of the Shadow Court and they are named after the event of when a person or object appears to have multiple shadows at once. Splintered Shadow grants powers of trickery, disguise, and stealth. The Shadow can appear to be in multiple places at once, or take on the appearance of someone else just to name a couple examples. Splintered Shadow is often used for when the Shadow Court does not wish to openly reveal their motives to others, and instead misleads them with false evidence. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T23:14:57-08:00","id":342673,"title":"","content":"Did the four courts of the medicine wheel, that went really well! Was thinking about using some Magic: the Gathering colors as courts. Also Types of vehicle, consoles, different types of rock (the stones), and different types of rock (music).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T05:21:14-08:00","id":342832,"title":"","content":"All cool ideas! Anyway, from what I can gather of that thread, the Outline thingy for the Huntsmen Chronicles will apparently have a system for designing Courts, so yeah, Awesome!<br /> <br /> Also, though I doubt anyone cares, I managed to come up with one more of my moon courts. As it stands, they're currently:<br /> \u2022New Moon<br /> \u2022Crescent Moon(Revelation)- Court of Shamans<br /> \u2022Half-Moon(Serenity)-Court of Counselors <br /> \u2022Gibbous Moon(Glory)-Court of Bards<br /> \u2022Full Moon(Restraint)-Court of Fetters<br /> Not to bug anyone, but anyone know anything that might fit the last one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T05:23:13-08:00","id":342834,"title":"","content":"Maybe Calmness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T05:34:37-08:00","id":342837,"title":"","content":"Quiescence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T06:45:47-08:00","id":342886,"title":"","content":"Thank you both for suggestions. Maybe if I combine them:<br /> \u2022New Moon(Patience)-Court of Stalkers<br /> \u2022Crescent Moon(Revelation)- Court of Shamans<br /> \u2022Half-Moon(Serenity)-Court of Counselors <br /> \u2022Gibbous Moon(Glory)-Court of Bards<br /> \u2022Full Moon(Restraint)- Court of Fetters<br /> <br /> Anyone think this looks good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T08:03:40-08:00","id":342917,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't a Court based on the moon phase shift it's governing body every few days? That could get rather hectic, I would imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T08:15:03-08:00","id":342921,"title":"","content":"While we're on the subject of &quot;food courts&quot; I had an idea for courts based on flavors.<br /> <br /> <br /> Court of Sourness (Courage) - Court of Risk Takers<br /> <br /> Court of Sweetness (Kindness) - Court of Companions<br /> <br /> Court of Bitterness (Spite) - Court of Avengers<br /> <br /> Court of Creaminess (Serenity) - Court of Mellow Souls<br /> <br /> <br /> No idea how they would govern, but it sounds like an amusing enough idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T08:25:38-08:00","id":342945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341338-fan-made-courts-any-ideas-you-have-or-want-to-see?p=342917#post342917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't a Court based on the moon phase shift it's governing body every few days? That could get rather hectic, I would imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, but it would probably prevent a Miami situation. Maybe make it a sort of Council with the ruling Court having more weight? <br /> <br /> As for the Flavor Courts... Maybe somewhere where most of the Lost belonged to culinarily themed Keepers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T21:01:54-08:00","id":343654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341338-fan-made-courts-any-ideas-you-have-or-want-to-see?p=341559#post341559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see a circus-based Freehold alternating between the Court of the Road (worry) while travelling and the court of the Ring (wonder) while in place for performances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally for this. A court that literally hides in plain site, with no questioning. Gaining glamour from the audiences, possibly dealing with other courts on a global scale . Being on the road makes it harder for them to pin down. Loyalist and privateers would have a hell of a time dealing with a court that was constantly on the move, and certainly works with crossover ideas with various splats.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T14:37:45-08:00","id":344115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nightout</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341338-fan-made-courts-any-ideas-you-have-or-want-to-see?p=343654#post343654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Totally for this. A court that literally hides in plain site, with no questioning. Gaining glamour from the audiences, possibly dealing with other courts on a global scale . Being on the road makes it harder for them to pin down. Loyalist and privateers would have a hell of a time dealing with a court that was constantly on the move, and certainly works with crossover ideas with various splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd certainly be an easy way to introduce them to a long-running Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Also, though I doubt anyone cares, I'm still working on the Virtue Courts. Added some titles and changed Chastity to Faith, mostly cause I couldn't think of a way to keep it different from Temperance, and I have more ideas for the later Court. <br /> Currently:<br /> \u2022Charity-Sunday's Court, Michael's Court, the Scale and the Sword, Court of Martyrs<br /> <br /> \u2022Kindness-Monday's Court, Gabriel's Court, the Trumpet and Lily, Court of Heralds<br /> <br /> \u2022Clarity- Tuesday's Court, Raphael's Court, the Pool and the Fish, Court of Shepards<br /> <br /> \u2022Faith- Wednesday's Court, Uriel's Court, the Scroll and the Flame, Court of Revealers<br /> <br /> \u2022Temperance- Thursday's Court, Cassiel's Court, the Eye and the Amulet, Court of Judges<br /> <br /> \u2022Diligence- Friday's Court, Jegudiel's <br /> Court, the Crown and the Whip, Court of Taskmasters<br /> <br /> \u2022Patience- Saturday's Court, Barachiel's Court, the Rose and the Storm, Court of Planners","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T15:32:13-08:00","id":344177,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for the Flower Courts. It never got far but maybe it will later. The flower courts are each defined by what kind of relationship they want with mortals. The four are:<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Balsam:</b> The Unyielding Flora, The Red Blossom, The Court of Stubbornness: Think Sheldon from the big bang theory, they think that having gone through trauma means they're entitled to sympathy and support (both financial and emotional) from everyone.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Honeysuckle</b> - The Choking Vine, The Pink Blossom, The Court of Dependency: Honeysuckles think that as Changelings they're inherently damaged and they want a human to fix them. They find a human that they love (or think they love) and change themselves to please that person.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Hollyhock</b> - The Proud Bloom, The Gold Blossom, The Court of Ambition: The Hollyhock court want success. Success is measured by fame and money, in that order. The True Fae made them nothing, and in response they're going to make themselves into something big.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Violet - </b>The Humble Herb, The Blue Blossom, The Court of Satisfaction: (shrinking) Violets are just happy that they're back on earth and not slaves. They've found a job or hobby that they enjoy and want to be left alone to do it quietly and in the safety of anonymity.<br /> <br /> Balsam and Honeysuckle form a pair - both are about close personal relationships but Balsam want others to change for them and Honeysuckle want to change for others.<br /> <br /> Hollyhock and Violet also form a pair - both are about impersonal relationships but Hollyhock want to be the big man on top and Violet want to be the overlooked office drone.<br /> <br /> Togeather this makes a 2-axis personal/impersonal selfish/selfless grid for the courts. Read &quot;selfish&quot; as a completely neutral word.<br /> <br /> Finally there's <b>The Lily Crown</b> - The Royal Flower, The White Blossom, The Crown: A single mortal selected by the Wyrd to rule the Freehold for one year. Lilly Kings and Queens are chosen specifically to lead the freehold for the good of the <u>mortals</u> in the Freehold's area, though a Lilly King who neglects internal Freehold matters is unlikely to get their courtiers to do more than the bare minimum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-19-2014, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T16:12:04-08:00","id":344204,"title":"","content":"@The Kings Raven: It certainly looks interesting. If I had to chose one, I'd lean towards Hollyhock or Violet myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T19:45:49-08:00","id":347112,"title":"","content":"Just had an idea, very bizarre. A Freehold based in Disneyland or Disneyworld's Magic Kingdom, based upon the original lands within. Not sure how this would work(are there employees who live on park lands?), but I like the idea. Here in Florida, the Courts would be;<br /> \u2022Tomorrowland(Wonder): Court of Innovation, <br /> \u2022Adventureland(Thrill): Court of Risks, <br /> \u2022Main Street, U.S.A.(Comfort): Court of Home<br /> \u2022Liberty Square(Remembrance): Court of Reverence<br /> \u2022Frontierland <br /> <br /> Presumably, each would rule their own section, with a council ruling the Freehold as a whole. Any thoughts, especially for Frontierland?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T16:35:02-08:00","id":347844,"title":"","content":"The Court of the Road. I wrote up part of this for the Onyx Path open writer call and my group demanded I finish it. So, voila! (Holler if the link doesn't work.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_NDcEF6Bn93LTlHZmxNN29EOVk/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_NDcEF6Bn93LTlHZmxNN29EOVk/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_NDcEF6Bn93LTlHZmxNN29EOVk/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_NDcEF6Bn93LTlHZmxNN29EOVk/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T16:35:39-08:00","id":347845,"title":"","content":"(DISTRESSED HOLLERING)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Never mind, it's fixed now. Will edit again once I've a chance to read it.<br /> <br /> EDIT2: I like it! It seems like a neat idea, and something interesting to include to a campaign. Just two questions; do they have any social groups, or are they just lone wolves? Also, what do they harvest for glamor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":". 12-23-2014, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T20:35:07-08:00","id":347966,"title":"","content":"Interesting! Is this a stand-alone Court of the Road with a different emotion, or is this tied to the &quot;Road and Ring&quot; circus court idea above?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T14:32:22-08:00","id":356934,"title":"","content":"If some Changelings understand that the Gentry are creatures of Story, then there might be some who can create Story-based Courts (Fantasy, Sci-Fi, Horror, Romance, etc). Though personally, I would like to see a Court system that emphasizes diplomatic relations with the other Supernatural denizens of the WoD.<br /> <br /> Blood Court: Deals with Vampires and the Court Contract helps the Changeling deal with the mercurial nuances of Kindred politics. (I can see this if the Changeling has a family member who is a Ghoul).<br /> Wyld Court: Deals with Werewolves. The Court Contract helps bolster the Changling physically from spiritual attacks.<br /> Arcane(?) Court: Deals with Mages. (I'm kind of lost (no pun intended) on what this Court's Contract would help them with because I don't want to push into Autumn Court territory here.)<br /> Wasted Court: Deals with Prometheans. (Again don't know what to do with the Contract, though I can see members of this Court gain the ability to harvest Glamour from Disquiet.)<br /> Death Court: Deals with Sin-Eaters. Court Contract assists Court member when they venture into the Underworld.<br /> Ancient Court: Deals with Mummies. (Again I don't know what to do for the Contract, but the same situation applies as with the Blood Court, only with cultists instead of Ghouls).<br /> Binary Court: Deals with Demons. (I think that the Contract here could help the Changeling use the same Exploits as Demons, but I would like input on this.)<br /> <br /> When Beast comes up, I can see a Court coming up to deal with this as well. Also, the reason why there's no Hunter Court is that, in Mortal Remains, Hunters see Changelings as normal humans with mental disorders (thanks to the Mask), so why rock the boat? <br /> <br /> Any ideas of Contracts, Emotions, etc. to improve this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T15:16:30-08:00","id":356963,"title":"","content":"@JackalopeVegas: Interesting idea, though I'd probably just make a local Court system inspired by other supernaturals. At the very least, it gives me an idea based on Courts focused on the different parts of the world(as Changelings know it). That is, a Court of the Twilight(as in the state of being, mostly dealing with spirits), a Court of the Underworld, the Court of the Hedge, and the Court of the Ironside(&quot;regular&quot; Earth).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T13:54:31-08:00","id":358550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341338-fan-made-courts-any-ideas-you-have-or-want-to-see?p=347966#post347966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting! Is this a stand-alone Court of the Road with a different emotion, or is this tied to the &quot;Road and Ring&quot; circus court idea above?</div> </div> </div> </div>This was meant as a standalone. Friends and I were contemplating a book just about itinerant changelings and it came to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T14:02:56-08:00","id":362856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341338-fan-made-courts-any-ideas-you-have-or-want-to-see?p=347845#post347845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it! It seems like a neat idea, and something interesting to include to a campaign. Just two questions; do they have any social groups, or are they just lone wolves? Also, what do they harvest for glamor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, missed the question before. I could have sworn that I put in their emotional resonance. Anyway, it is restlessness or discontent. They get glamour from people who are looking for a change, who aren't happy where they are. This is why they have a reputation for being a bad influence when the come to town, they tend to rile people up and get them to think about where they would rather be.<br /> <br /> As for social groups, their monarchs' power depends on numbers, so they tend to be jealous of their membership and encourage clannish behavior. Usually they will form a group (a biker gang, a travelling circus, a touring band, a &quot;family&quot; etc) with its own traditions, rules, and customs binding them together and cultivating wariness towards &quot;outsiders&quot;. On the other hand are individuals sworn to the court but on their own, but I see them as getting a lot of pressure to join Dirt Court groups they cross paths with.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T16:24:37-08:00","id":373916,"title":"","content":"Another idea to add to the &quot;throw out and then ignore 'till 2e and its Court-making rules come out&quot; pile. A particular variation on the idea of the Seasonal Courts dating back to the first Egyptian Lost.<br /> <br /> ~Nile Courts<br /> \u2022Aketo(Flooding): Court of Anticipation, They who rush, the Warrior's Court<br /> <br /> \u2022Peret(Growing): Court of Toil, They who tend, the Worker's Court<br /> <br /> \u2022Syumuu(Harvesting): Court of Catharsis, They who reap, the Court of Priests <br /> <br /> Each basically rules according to their traditional time in the old Egyptian calender; there is no &quot;Court of Kings&quot; to avoid questionibg the authority of the Pharaoh(with instead each Court having it's own name for the ruler) and to ensure people remember the exchange of power, which many Changelings then and now believe ensure the fertility of the land just as much as the actual flood cycle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T19:17:59-08:00","id":387922,"title":"","content":"So I'm working on another changeling campaign and I'm thinking of playing up the Hellraiser/Midian angle with it. My general thoughts are to make courts based on monstrous archetypes, possibly Sumerian - like Tiamat (creativeness? Mother-ess-ness?), Girtablilu (Hedge stuff?), Enkidu (physical court of revelry and drunkenness?), and so on. Guess is only needs three, but I'm into the number four as a cycle.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T17:42:18-08:00","id":389155,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see something with Las Vegas and the four suits of the modern playing card deck, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suit_(cards)\" target=\"_blank\">which has a lot of history</a>. Hearts would be entertainers (of all stripes), Diamonds would be the monied folk and gamblers, Clubs would be your pit bosses and hotel maids, and Spades would be the classic &quot;criminal element&quot; of classic 50s Vegas. Who gets to be king? It's all in the luck of the draw, I say.<br /> <br /> I'm also working on a &quot;times of the day&quot; group of Courts, with each time of day corresponding to an aspect of story structure. Dawn involves Beginnings, Noonday is Revelations, Dusk evokes the Desperation of the second act turn, and Midnight are the weavers of plot who are <i>trying to get things done </i>while nobody's looking. It's weird and rough and Dawn/Dusk have been done before, but I kinda like it and may post it when I get through with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T17:58:23-08:00","id":389174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341338-fan-made-courts-any-ideas-you-have-or-want-to-see?p=389155#post389155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see something with Las Vegas and the four suits of the modern playing card deck, <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suit_(cards)&amp;quot;]which</a> has a lot of history[/URL]. Hearts would be entertainers (of all stripes), Diamonds would be the monied folk and gamblers, Clubs would be your pit bosses and hotel maids, and Spades would be the classic &amp;quot;criminal element&amp;quot; of classic 50s Vegas. Who gets to be king? It's all in the luck of the draw, I say.</div> </div> </div> </div> While it's not exactly what you layed out, someone over at Rpg.net made some headway into a Las Vegas Suits Freehold. The fruits of his labor are recorded here: <a href=\"http://lostvegas.pbworks.com/w/page/...egas%20Society\" target=\"_blank\">http://lostvegas.pbworks.com/w/page/...egas%20Society</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T15:21:29-08:00","id":391927,"title":"","content":"I started typing up the other day two Courts that at first seem to oppose each other, but gradually change into the philosophies of the other over time. For now calling them the Court of the Seed and the Court of the Cog. May post soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}